course: dictionary
lesson: 14703
title: The word prior
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Prior is a formal word, the kind you find in exams and official letters. It means earlier, or before something else. «Prior to the race, she had 10 dollars.» Prior to the race means before the race, so she had the money before she ran.
explain: Prior often appears in set phrases. «No prior knowledge is needed for this quiz» means you do not need to know anything about it already. Prior knowledge is what you know before you start, and prior experience is what you have done before.
explain: Use the swap test to check. Put "before" into the sentence: «before the race» still makes sense, so prior means before.
fact: Prior means happening or existing before something else; earlier.
fact: «Prior to» is a formal phrase that means before, as in «prior to lunch».
fact: «Prior knowledge» means what you already know before you learn something new.
fact: «Prior experience» means things you have done before.
fact: A prior is also a noun: the head of a group of monks or a priory.
exercise: «Prior to the match, the team had practised every day.» What does prior to mean here? | After the match | During the match | *Before the match | Instead of the match
exercise: «No prior experience is needed to join the club.» What does prior experience mean? | Being the team leader | A long list of games | Experience you get after joining | *Things you have done before
exercise: Ravi says prior means pretty. What does prior really mean? | Lovely to look at | Very loud | Sorry for something you did | *Earlier, or before something else
test: Which word is closest in meaning to prior? | Final | *Earlier | Later | Future
test: Fill the gap: Please read the rules ___ the game starts. | Until | After | Since | *Prior to
exam: Which phrase means the same as «before the bell»? | *Prior to the bell | Beside the bell | After the bell | Ringing the bell
